{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/violence-against-women",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "violence against women"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Any act of gender-based violence that causes or is likely to cause women physical, sexual, psychological or economic harm or suffering, including threats, coercion or arbitrary deprivation of liberty, in public or private life."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "It is directed against a woman because she is a woman or affects women disproportionately; it is both a form of discrimination and a human rights violation, rooted in unequal power relations. It covers manifestations such as domestic, sexual, obstetric or vicarious violence, as well as harmful practices such as female genital mutilation. For women and girls with disabilities, it takes specific and aggravated forms – forced sterilisation or treatment, institutional violence or violence by caregivers – and intersects with disability-based discrimination; hence the need for reinforced measures of prevention, protection, accessibility and access to justice (art. 16 CRPD)."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "13.8"
  ],
